{"chunk_id": "35f0162b128a", "text": "After Sita\u2019s abduction, Rama struggles with rage and despair until Lakshmana urges him to search the wild and demon\u2011haunted region of Janasthana. As they comb the forest, Rama discovers the giant vulture king Jatayu lying bloodied on the ground and initially assumes the bird is a demon who has devoured Sita. Preparing to kill him, Rama is stopped when the dying Jatayu speaks. The vulture reveals that Ravana abducted Sita and that he himself fought the demon king in the sky, smashing his chariot and killing his charioteer before Ravana severed his wings and escaped with Sita. Overcome with grief and gratitude, Rama embraces the dying bird, lamenting his fate and mourning his father\u2019s old friend. The scene is pivotal because it confirms Ravana as Sita\u2019s abductor and frames Jatayu\u2019s heroic resistance as a noble sacrifice.\nRama and Lakshmana discover the mortally wounded Jatayu, who reveals Ravana abducted Sita after he tried to rescue her.\nThemes: loyalty and sacrifice, grief and despair, revelation of Sita's abduction, heroic resistance to evil", "vector": [-0.005519914906471968, -0.026270341128110886, -0.007543228566646576, 0.003016964066773653, -0.024672644212841988, 0.018399715423583984, -0.029649078845977783, -0.022145139053463936, -0.01838661916553974, -0.030827708542346954, 0.015505525283515453, 0.01427451241761446, 0.006292571779340506, 0.007183091714978218, -0.0027812381740659475, -0.004783271346241236, 0.04455219581723213, -0.008610542863607407, 0.03771614283323288, -0.016802018508315086, -0.00046326685696840286, -0.011380322277545929, -0.02247253619134426, 0.006079763639718294, -0.005624681711196899, 1.6791889720479958e-05, 0.015099553391337395, -0.03632798045873642, 0.029884805902838707, -0.006364599335938692, -0.016265086829662323, -0.008558159694075584, -0.0196831114590168, -0.011733911000192165, -0.015911497175693512, 0.013960211537778378, 0.009920131415128708, -0.014235224574804306, 0.0102